insert into sat_private.questions(id,version,document,option_id,explanation) values
('bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e01',1,'{"id":"bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e01","version":1,"section":"rw","skillId":"3811ef86-8bf0-41cf-a301-600e20d54e01","difficulty":"medium","format":"multiple-choice","language":"en","provenance":{"kind":"original","author":"SAT Study OS — conteúdo original"},"passage":"In a coastal town, researchers planted native grasses on two sections of a damaged dune. One section was fenced to keep visitors off the young plants; the other remained open. After a year, the fenced section had denser vegetation, although both sections had received similar amounts of rain. The researchers noted that roots help hold sand in place, but that newly planted grasses are easily damaged by foot traffic.","prompt":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the researchers’ explanation for the difference between the two sections?","options":[{"id":"a","label":"A","text":"The fenced section experienced fewer instances of plants being stepped on than the open section did."},{"id":"b","label":"B","text":"The two sections were planted with the same number of native grass species."},{"id":"c","label":"C","text":"Visitors preferred to visit the beach in summer rather than in winter."},{"id":"d","label":"D","text":"Some native grasses can grow in coastal towns with less annual rainfall."}]}'::jsonb,'a','Foot traffic damages young grasses. Fewer plants being stepped on in the fenced section directly supports that mechanism. Similar species or seasonal preferences do not explain the difference.'),
('bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e02',1,'{"id":"bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e02","version":1,"section":"rw","skillId":"3811ef86-8bf0-41cf-a301-600e20d54e02","difficulty":"easy","format":"multiple-choice","language":"en","provenance":{"kind":"original","author":"SAT Study OS — conteúdo original"},"passage":"While studying old maps of the valley, geographer Lina Costa noticed that a narrow stream appeared in records from several different decades. Its course was remarkably consistent: despite changes to nearby roads and farms, the stream followed almost exactly the same path.","prompt":"As used in the text, “consistent” most nearly means","options":[{"id":"a","label":"A","text":"persuasive."},{"id":"b","label":"B","text":"unchanging."},{"id":"c","label":"C","text":"unexpected."},{"id":"d","label":"D","text":"complex."}]}'::jsonb,'b','The stream followed almost exactly the same path despite nearby changes. In this context, consistent means unchanging, rather than persuasive, unexpected, or complex.'),
('bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e03',1,'{"id":"bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e03","version":1,"section":"rw","skillId":"3811ef86-8bf0-41cf-a301-600e20d54e03","difficulty":"medium","format":"multiple-choice","language":"en","provenance":{"kind":"original","author":"SAT Study OS — conteúdo original"},"passage":"Most of the seedlings in a greenhouse grew slowly during the first week of an experiment. One group, however, received additional light each evening. ______ these seedlings grew nearly twice as tall as the others by the end of the week.","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":[{"id":"a","label":"A","text":"Nevertheless,"},{"id":"b","label":"B","text":"For instance,"},{"id":"c","label":"C","text":"As a result,"},{"id":"d","label":"D","text":"In contrast to this result,"}]}'::jsonb,'c','Additional light is presented as the cause of the extra growth. As a result connects the cause to its outcome; the other options imply contrast or an example.'),
('bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e04',1,'{"id":"bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e04","version":1,"section":"rw","skillId":"3811ef86-8bf0-41cf-a301-600e20d54e04","difficulty":"medium","format":"multiple-choice","language":"en","provenance":{"kind":"original","author":"SAT Study OS — conteúdo original"},"passage":"A community archive preserves recordings of local musicians ______ volunteers also maintain written descriptions of each performance.","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[{"id":"a","label":"A","text":"and,"},{"id":"b","label":"B","text":","},{"id":"c","label":"C","text":";"},{"id":"d","label":"D","text":"because,"}]}'::jsonb,'c','Both sides are independent clauses. A semicolon joins them correctly. A comma alone creates a comma splice; the other options misplace punctuation.'),
('bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e05',1,'{"id":"bb5d789f-5ae6-4670-a301-600e20d54e05","version":1,"section":"rw","skillId":"3811ef86-8bf0-41cf-a301-600e20d54e01","difficulty":"hard","format":"multiple-choice","language":"en","provenance":{"kind":"original","author":"SAT Study OS — conteúdo original"},"passage":"A city library extended its evening opening hours for three months. During that period, evening attendance increased, but the total number of weekly visits remained approximately the same. A librarian suggested that many visitors had changed the time of their visits rather than begun visiting more often.","prompt":"Which statement is best supported by the information in the text?","options":[{"id":"a","label":"A","text":"The extended hours caused all daytime visitors to stop using the library."},{"id":"b","label":"B","text":"The library’s collection became less popular during the three-month period."},{"id":"c","label":"C","text":"Evening visitors borrowed more books per visit than daytime visitors did."},{"id":"d","label":"D","text":"The increase in evening attendance did not necessarily represent an increase in weekly visits."}]}'::jsonb,'d','Evening attendance rose while weekly visits stayed roughly constant. The increase can reflect visits shifting to another time. The passage does not establish the claims about all visitors, the collection, or borrowing per visit.');
